        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this bright and spacious three bedroom semi-detached family home to the market situated in the extremely sought after cul de sac of Clonsilla Park, D15. Clonsilla Park is located in the popular suburb of Blanchardstown and is situated close to a wealth of amenities including schools, shops and recreational facilities. Nearby amenities include Castleknock Golf and Country Club, St. Brigids GAA Club, Castleknock Lawn Tennis Club, Blanchardstown and Roselawn Shopping Centres, and the Phoenix Park which offers many outdoor pursuits. The area is well-serviced by public transport: Dublin Bus provides a regular service for the area; and Castleknock train station is approximately a 5-minute walk away. The M50, which provides access to the national road network, is just a few minutes' drive away.\nBright and spacious, this light-filled home extends to approximately 110 sq.m and offers well-proportioned living accommodation throughout. The ground floor comprises an entrance hallway, a cosy lounge with fireplace, a fully fitted kitchen, and a separate dining room. Just off the kitchen is a large converted garage, ideal for additional storage or a variety of other uses. Upstairs features three generous double bedrooms and a main family bathroom. No. 6 further benefits from a large sunny rear garden with a desirable west-facing orientation, as well as ample off-street parking to the front. Presented with no onward chain, the property offers excellent potential to create the perfect family home in a prestigious and highly sought-after location. Additional features include extensive built-in storage, spacious room proportions, a converted garage, large attic space with possibility of attic conversion and a quiet cul-de-sac setting.\n\n\nFeatures;\n- 3 Bed, 2 Bath Semi D\n- BER D2\n- c.110 sq.m\n-Garage conversion\n-Gas fired central heating\n-Huge potential\n-Large attic space\n-West facing rear garden\n-Quiet cul de sac\n-Ample parking\n-Mature & sought after location\n-Excellent primary & secondary schools in the area\n-Bus routes & train station to City centre close by\n-Walking distance of Castleknock & Blanchardstown Villages\n-Easy access to M50 motorway\n-No onward chain\n-Early viewing highly advised!"
      },
      {
